# title: Automatic farm
# description: Plants a field, waits for it to grow, harvests, puts the harvest in the chest behind it and starts again.
# Setup: the robot hovers one block above the first crop square of the field (it needs a
# Hover Upgrade: crops are in the way of a robot on the ground), facing along the first
# row. A chest stands right behind it. Soil below the crop squares. Put the seeds in the
# robot's storage. Change the lines under "settings" to your crop.
use farming
use waypoint

# --- settings ---
set width = 6
set rows = 4
set seed = "farming:seed_wheat"
set crop = "farming:wheat"
set grow_time = 3000

# harvest a field the way farming.plant_field plants it
fn harvest_field w d
  repeat d
    call farming.harvest_row w
    if even counter
      turn right
      move forward
      turn right
    else
      turn left
      move forward
      turn left

fn home
  call waypoint.go_face "start"

# the start place: where the robot is now
call waypoint.save "start"
forever
  call farming.plant_field width rows seed
  call home
  wait grow_time
  call harvest_field width rows
  call home
  # the harvest into the chest behind (the seeds stay)
  turn around
  loop contains crop
    put crop
  turn around
